ints` (Route DENSE) | `Dense {p | ∃ x ∈ orbitSet M, p = pointIdeal x}` in `Spec A`. | REUSE `zeroLocus_vanishingIdeal_eq_closure`, `zeroLocus_bot`, landed L6 ideal equality. BUILD: the single lemma `vanishingIdeal{orbit closed points} = ⊥` (CHEAP) + the closed-point/maximal-ideal dictionary glue. | ~1 module |\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/34-A2-l3-smoothness-api/findings.md:169:**`vanishingIdeal {orbit closed points} = ⊥` in `A`** (Route DENSE's L3.3 core) — but this is CHEAP\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/34-A2-l3-smoothness-api/findings.md:197:- Route DENSE's `vanishingIdeal{orbit closed points} = ⊥` assumes the orbit-closed-points are the\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/34-A2-l3-smoothness-api/findings.md:198:  k-rational maximal ideals and that L6 is delivered as a `vanishingIdeal` equality (it is). If L6\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/34-A2-l3-smoothness-api/findings.md:199:  delivers only set-equality of closures, add one `congrArg vanishingIdeal` (thread-29 L1' already\n./expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/threads/14-r1-design/codex/g121-C1-vs-C2-answer.md:41:**FACT.** A general blow-up of a non-coordinate ideal, e.g. the ideal \\((r-pq)\\) or a determinantal/rank-defect ideal, is a different construction from coordinate-subspace blow-up.\n./expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/threads/14-r1-design/codex/g121-C1-vs-C2-answer.md:45:**INFERENCE.** If Lean had a separate, fully developed theory of blow-ups along arbitrary smooth centers or determinantal ideals, then one could try to eliminate the explicit Schur step by treating the bilinear center directly. But that is not the chosen machinery. With the present coordinate-subspace machinery, the bilinear center must first be straightened.\n./expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/threads/14-r1-design/codex/g121-C1-vs-C2-answer.md:47:**INFERENCE.** A sequence of coordinate-subspace blow-ups in the original unstraightened coordinates should not be expected to resolve the matrix-chain rank-defect geometry cleanly. The Schur operation is what keeps the recursive centers coordinate after a unit pivot has been chosen. Without it, the centers become Schur-complement equations such as \\(r-pq=0\\), then higher determinantal analogues, which are not coordinate subspaces in the ambient chart coordinates.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/34-A2-l3-smoothness-api/codex/crux-prompt.md:10:- `orbitRankLocus M = {A | ∀ i≤j, rankPattern A i j ≤ rankPattern M i j}` — determinantal locus.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/34-A2-l3-smoothness-api/codex/crux-prompt.md:14:- `vanishingIdeal (canonicalCoord '' orbitRankLocus M) = vanishingIdeal (orbitSet M)` (L6, the\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/34-A2-l3-smoothness-api/codex/crux-prompt.md:16:- `isPrime_vanishingIdeal_orbitRankLocus` ⟹ `A := MvPolynomial(RepCoord d) k / vanishingIdeal(Z_M)`\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/34-A2-l3-smoothness-api/codex/crux-prompt.md:45:   CLOSED (determinantal). So `Z_M \\ O_M` is closed in `Z_M`, hence `O_M` is OPEN in `Z_M`. Is this\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/34-A2-l3-smoothness-api/codex/crux-prompt.md:46:   correct? Pitfall: \"rank ≤ r−1\" is closed (determinantal, fewer minors vanish... no: rank ≤ r−1\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/34-A2-l3-smoothness-api/codex/crux-prompt.md:47:   means MORE minors vanish, so it IS closed — a determinantal locus). So O_M = Z_M minus a finite\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/34-A2-l3-smoothness-api/codex/crux-prompt.md:48:   union of determinantal closed sets = open in Z_M. Does this hold, and does it transfer to\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/34-A2-l3-smoothness-api/codex/crux-prompt.md:57:   move: define everything via the determinantal IDEALS on the ring side (the lower-rank loci as\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/34-A2-l3-smoothness-api/codex/crux-prompt.md:78:crux to a clean determinantal-ideal computation, say so and sketch the exact ideal-theoretic\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/34-A2-l3-smoothness-api/codex/crux-answer.md:9:where `A = R ⧸ I`, `R = MvPolynomial (RepCoord d) k`, `I = vanishingIdeal k (canonicalCoord '' orbitRankLocus M)`, and `m_x` is the quotient maximal ideal induced by evaluation at the orbit point `x`.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/34-A2-l3-smoothness-api/codex/crux-answer.md:18:theorem dense_orbitClosedPoints_of_vanishingIdeal_eq\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/34-A2-l3-smoothness-api/codex/crux-answer.md:19:    (hI : vanishingIdeal k (orbitSet M)\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/34-A2-l3-smoothness-api/codex/crux-answer.md:20:        = vanishingIdeal k (canonicalCoord d '' orbitRankLocus M)) :\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/34-A2-l3-smoothness-api/codex/crux-answer.md:24:Proof idea: `p` ranges over kernels of lifted evaluations `A →ₐ[k] k`. The vanishing ideal of these points in `A` is `⊥`, because a representative polynomial vanishes on all orbit points iff it lies in `vanishingIdeal (orbitSet M) = I`. Hence their closure is `V(⊥)=Spec A`.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/34-A2-l3-smoothness-api/codex/crux-answer.md:44:is itself an `orbitRankLocus` of a smaller tuple. It is a determinantal closed locus; that is enough. The modified rank pattern may not be realizable as one tuple’s full rank pattern.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/34-A2-l3-smoothness-api/codex/crux-answer.md:78:PrimeSpectrum.vanishingIdeal orbitClosedPointsInQuotient = ⊥\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:1:# Thread 21 — route sizing: determinantal-KMS (a) vs orbit-stabiliser/Chevalley (b) [pen-and-paper, 2026-06-19]\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:3:## VERDICT: ROUTE (a) smooth-point assembly — smaller by a large factor. KMS determinantal sub-library AVOIDED.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:8:  `dim source = dim target + dim fibre` in any form. Orbit-dimension package ABSENT. `ringKrullDim = trdeg` for\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:9:  f.g. domain/field ABSENT (so even the trdeg-additivity route to (b) is blocked). ⟹ route (b) = a from-scratch\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:14:- **Determinantal PRIMENESS (KMS/Lakshmibai–Magyar) NOT needed.** Take `I = vanishingIdeal(Z_M)` directly —\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:15:  prime from `isPrime_vanishingIdeal_orbitSet` (O_M irreducible, LANDED) + `Z_M = Ō_M` (L6). The cotangent/regular\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:16:  chain runs on the reduced ring; never need \"(minors) = vanishingIdeal\".\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:18:  (intrinsic). NOT via minor pderivs (that would re-import determinantal primeness — guard K2: use dμ_M=δ⁰).\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:21:`varietyDim(Z_M) =[L4d] ringKrullDim(AtPrime m_M) =[M3 smooth⟹regular] finrank(cotangent) =[L2a, LANDED]\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:27:- L6.3 easy direction (rank lower-semicontinuity, Ō_M ⊆ Z_M) ☐ module. L6.4 `vanishingIdeal(Z_M)=vanishingIdeal(O_M)`\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:28:  ideal-level ☐ module (reuses `vanishingIdeal_range_orbitMap_eq_ker`). L1 `(vanishingIdeal Z_M).IsPrime` ☐ short.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-answer.md:3:1. **No.** Chevalley constructibility exists (`PrimeSpectrum.isConstructible_comap_image`, `Scheme.Hom.isConstructible_image`), and trdeg