findings.md:15:  vanishingIdeal(Z_M)`; L2a needs `I_minors = vanishingIdeal(Z_M)` (radical/prime). That is the **equioriented\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/findings.md:16:  type-A quiver determinantal-ideal primeness theorem (Lakshmibai–Magyar Thm 2.2 / Knutson–Miller–Shimozono)** —\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/findings.md:17:  absent in Mathlib v4.29 (matrix minors/rank/Cotangent/Kähler present; NO quiver-determinantal prime/reduced/CM\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/findings.md:20:  determinantal-stratum tangent + barcode/gauge count) is itself a local sub-library on top of the generation gate.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/findings.md:28:`vanishingIdeal(Z_M) = (interval-subproduct minors)` as a prime/radical IDEAL — the Lakshmibai–Magyar/KMS theorem.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/findings.md:29:Gates the determinantal route entirely.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/findings.md:33:### Recommended: SURFACE the scope surprise; pick the sub-library. (a) quiver-determinantal-ideal (Lakshmibai–\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/findings.md:34:Magyar/KMS — SHARES cost with L6, reuses landed `vanishingIdeal(O_M)=ker μ_M^*` + L2a/L4★ → lower marginal cost)\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/codex/l2b-answer.md:3:**(B)** SUB-LIBRARY. FACT: the interval-subproduct minors define the same set as `Z_M`; by Nullstellensatz this gives `vanishingIdeal(Z_M) = radical(I_minors)`, not `I_minors` itself. FACT: L2a needs the stronger scheme-theoretic statement `I_minors = vanishingIdeal(Z_M)`, equivalently radicality/reducedness, and then primeness follows from irreducibility. FACT: for equioriented type A this is the quiver determinantal ideal theorem: orbit closures/quiver loci are scheme-theoretically cut out by these minors and are reduced/Cohen-Macaulay/prime, via Lakshmibai-Magyar/Zelevinsky or Knutson-Miller-Shimozono-type quiver determinantal theory. ([arxiv.org](https://arxiv.org/abs/alg-geom/9709018)) Mathlib v4.29 likely has matrix determinants/rank and commutative algebra infrastructure, but not this quiver determinantal ideal theory.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/codex/l2b-answer.md:5:**(C)** FACT: given the minors, their Jacobian kernel at `M` is the first-order rank-preserving condition for every interval product: for each product `F`, the perturbation `H` satisfies `H(ker F) ⊆ im F`. FACT: in barcode/interval normal form this can be solved uniformly: the interval conditions kill exactly the Ext¹ directions, leaving precisely coboundaries `δ⁰(φ)`. INFERENCE: this is not per-orbit ad hoc, but it is bar/lace-parametrized uniform linear algebra; formalising it still needs a substantial local sub-library: tangent space of determinantal rank strata, differential of subproducts, barcode block decomposition, and the gauge-elimination/Voigt computation.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/codex/l2b-answer.md:11:Verdict: the smallest non-circular route to `varietyDim(Z_M)=finrank(range δ⁰)` is orbit-stabilizer-dimension; determinantal-Jacobian is viable but heavier, and smoothness-only is insufficient. None is bounded in Mathlib v4.29; each real route pulls a missing sub-library.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/codex/l2b-prompt.md:8:  polynomial orbit map μ_M : G → Rep_d, P ↦ P·M). We have PROVED: vanishingIdeal(O_M) = ker(μ_M^*),\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/codex/l2b-prompt.md:24:  REQUIREMENT: g must generate I = vanishingIdeal(Z_M) as an ideal (the family enters as\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/codex/l2b-prompt.md:29:A