oof via determinantal CA is the **larger** build\" — needs polynomial rings,\n./expeditions/2026-06-17-ext-codimension/threads/04-rankloc-probe/scratch.md:81:minors, determinantal/Schubert ideals, radical/prime/height, standard-monomial or Gröbner theory, AND\n./expeditions/2026-06-17-ext-codimension/threads/04-rankloc-probe/scratch.md:83:Lean formalization, I would not start with quiver determinantal CA.\" The algebraic-group/orbit-dimension\n./expeditions/2026-06-17-ext-codimension/threads/04-rankloc-probe/scratch.md:90:Cohen–Macaulay determinantal ideal; = Buch–Fulton rectangle sum = dim Ext¹). It is NOT computable by the\n./expeditions/2026-06-17-ext-codimension/threads/04-rankloc-probe/scratch.md:91:cheap regular-sequence/Eagon–Northcott route — it is an excess/non-CI quiver-determinantal height. As a\n./expeditions/2026-06-17-ext-codimension/threads/04-rankloc-probe/scratch.md:92:Lean build it is LARGER than the algebraic-group orbit-dimension route, not smaller. The determinantal-CA\n./expeditions/2026-06-17-ext-codimension/threads/04-rankloc-probe/scratch.md:93:route does NOT shrink Layer 2; it relocates the ocean (from AG to Schubert/quiver determinantal CA +\n./expeditions/2026-06-17-ext-codimension/threads/04-rankloc-probe/codex/rankloc-prompt.md:9:sequences, determinantal ideal heights, Eagon-Northcott, Cohen-Macaulayness) WITHOUT invoking\n./expeditions/2026-06-17-ext-codimension/threads/04-rankloc-probe/codex/rankloc-prompt.md:18:(2) Is the CODIMENSION of this rank locus in Rep_d computable by classical determinantal CA?\n./expeditions/2026-06-17-ext-codimension/threads/04-rankloc-probe/codex/rankloc-prompt.md:19:    I.e. is codim Ō_M = sum of determinantal-height contributions, via a known regular sequence /\n./expeditions/2026-06-17-ext-codimension/threads/04-rankloc-probe/codex/rankloc-prompt.md:20:    determinantal ideal height theorem, so that one could in principle PROVE codim = dim Ext^1(M,M)\n./expeditions/2026-06-17-ext-codimension/threads/04-