but I found no fibre-dimension theorem / Stacks `02FZ`, `02NM`, `05F6`-usable declaration.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-answer.md:10:   - **(b3) Partial, not enough.** Trdeg and Noether normalization exist (`trdeg_add_eq`, `NoetherNormalization.exists_finite_inj_algHom_of_fg` `[stacks 00OW]`), but I found no `ringKrullDim = trdeg` theorem for finitely generated domains.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-answer.md:12:4. **No.** Matrix minors/rank infrastructure exists (`Matrix.submatrix`, `Matrix.det`, `Matrix.rank`, `Matrix.rank_submatrix_le`), but I found no determinantal-ideal primeness/radical/CM theory, variety-of-complexes, or quiver-locus ideal package.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-answer.md:14:5. **Decision: route (a) is the smaller remaining Lean build, likely by a large factor.** Given your landed smooth/local/Jacobian bedrock, route (a) can avoid full determinantal-ideal primeness if `Z_M = closure O_M` is proved set-theoretically: `O_M` irreducible implies `Z_M` irreducible/prime, and homogeneity plus dense smooth locus gives smoothness of `M`; the genuinely new content is then `Z_M = closure O_M`, smoothness via homogeneity, and `ker Jac_M = range δ⁰`. Route (b) would require building Chevalley fibre dimension plus an algebraic orbit-dimension layer essentially from scratch.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-answer.md:16:Caveat: the Jacobian step must compare the cotangent space of the reduced/prime `Z_M` with the chosen minor equations. That does **not** require global determinantal primeness, but it does require either using the vanishing ideal in the bridge or proving the minor generators give the correct first-order equations at `M`.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-answer.md:18:6. **Sharpest risk: `Z_M = closure O_M` for equioriented type A.** It balloons if formalized as scheme-theoretic/radical ideal equality or via full Lakshmibai-Magyar/KMS determinantal primeness; keep it as a set-theoretic degeneration-order theorem plus a separate first-order Jacobian lemma.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-stdout.log:29:- The polynomial-ring catenary/dimension formula `height p + ringKrullDim(R/p) = n` for R = k[x_1..x_n].\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-stdout.log:30:- An affine-domain dimension formula `height p + ringKrullDim(A/p) = ringKrullDim A` and\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-stdout.log:31:  local↔global `ringKrullDim(Localization.AtPrime m) = ringKrullDim A` for a finite-type domain A.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-stdout.log:39:- O_M is Zariski-irreducible; the orbit map; vanishingIdeal(image orbit map) = ker(orbit-map pullback).\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-stdout.log:45:ROUTE (a) — \"determinantal / smooth-point\" assembly. Via the landed bridges:\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-stdout.log:46:  varietyDim(Z_M) = ringKrullDim(AtPrime m_M)       [affine-domain local↔global; needs Z_M prime]\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-stdout.log:54:  (the equioriented type-A quiver determinantal-ideal primeness theorem — Lakshmibai–Magyar / Knutson–\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-stdout.log:71:   form usable for affine varieties / finite-type domains over a field (e.g. ringKrullDim relating a\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-stdout.log:72:   morphism's source, target, and fibre; trdeg =