olynomial.aeval a_M`. The Leibniz proof is exactly `DualNumber.snd_mul` plus the equality `(TrivSqZeroExt.fstHom k k k).comp (MvPolynomial.aeval pε) = MvPolynomial.aeval a_M`, proved by `MvPolynomial.algHom_ext`. Then identify it with `MvPolynomial.mkDerivation k v` using `MvPolynomial.derivation_ext` and `MvPolynomial.mkDerivation_X`. Secret Lean break: without explicitly setting the `R`-action on `k` through `aeval a_M`, the statement “`g` is a derivation” is ill-typed or has the wrong Leibniz rule. Also, if `orbitIdeal` is the repo’s `vanishingIdeal orbitSet`, Step B needs `range_orbitMap` + `vanishingIdeal_range_orbitMap_eq_ker`, not just `RingHom.mem_ker`.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/37-A4-orbit-image-dim/codex/a42-core-prompt.md:4:independent\" criterion, specialised to give trdeg ≤ differential-span-rank.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/37-A4-orbit-image-dim/codex/a42-core-prompt.md:8:  genericDifferentialRank := finrank K (Submodule.span K (Set.range fun i ↦ D k K (algebraMap B K (f i))))\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/37-A4-orbit-image-dim/codex/a42-core-prompt.md:12:  (Algebra.trdeg k (Algebra.adjoin k (Set.range f))).toNat ≤ genericDifferentialRank\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/37-A4-orbit-image-dim/codex/a42-core-prompt.md:13:i.e. trdeg of the subalgebra generated by f ≤ the K-rank of the span of {D(f_i)} in Ω[K⁄k].\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/37-A4-orbit-image-dim/codex/a42-core-prompt.md:21:- Algebra.trdeg, IsTranscendenceBasis, exists_isTranscendenceBasis, IsTranscendenceBasis.cardinalMk_eq_trdeg,\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/37-A4-orbit-image-dim/codex/a42-core-prompt.md:22:  trdeg_add_eq, MvPolynomial.trdeg_of_isDomain, trdeg_eq_zero, KaehlerDifferential.mvPolynomialBasis,\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/37-A4-orbit-image-dim/codex/a42-core-prompt.md:27:The differentials {D(f_i)} live in Ω[K⁄k] and I want: a max