 GENERIC rank (over Frac B) is what equals trdeg, not the rank at an arbitrary special point.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-prompt.md:40:           generic-smoothness theorem to say \"generic differential rank = dim image = trdeg\"?\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-prompt.md:41:      (iii) Flag clearly: which of the two facts (trdeg = generic Jacobian rank) and (generic rank = rank\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-prompt.md:46:    Algebra.trdeg as a Cardinal, IsTranscendenceBasis, AlgebraicIndependent, trdeg_add_eq tower,\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-prompt.md:47:    trdeg_le_of_injective, KaehlerDifferential.finite; it does NOT have any lemma connecting\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-prompt.md:48:    AlgebraicIndependent/trdeg with pderiv/Jacobian rank, nor \"rank Ω_{L/k} = trdeg L\" for field\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-prompt.md:50:    \"trdeg ≤ generic Jacobian rank\" criterion SECRETLY require first proving the field-extension fact\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-prompt.md:51:    \"dim_L Ω_{L/k} = trdeg_k L\" (a structure theorem Mathlib lacks)? I want an honest answer on whether\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-prompt.md:57:  A1 — the criterion + proof of trdeg ≤ generic rank (and = if cheap), char-0 usage pinpointed.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-prompt.md:61:       trdeg for fields?\" verdict.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-prompt.md:62:  A4 — one-paragraph bottom line: is the trdeg ≤ rank δ⁰ bound sound as I've framed it, and what is the\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-answer.md:3:Let `K = Frac(B)` and `F = Frac(A) = k(f_1,...,f_n) ⊆ K`. By definition `trdeg_k(A) = trdeg_k(F)`.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-answer.md:52:so `F/E` is algebraic and `r = trdeg_k(F)`.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-answer.md:63:trdeg_k(A) = r ≤ rank_K span(df_1,...,df_n).\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-answer.md:77:trdeg_k k[f_1,...,f_n]\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-answer.md:90:The characteristic-zero/separability point is essential. In characteristic `p`, with `B = k[x]` and `f = x^p`, one has `trdeg_k k[x^p] = 1` but `df = d(x^p) = 0`, so the generic Jacobian rank is `0`.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-answer.md:155:trdeg = generic Jacobian rank\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-answer.md:164:is characteristic-free for smooth groups and equivariant maps. It can hold in characteristic `p` even while `trdeg = generic rank` fails; e.g. `G_m` acting on `A^1` by the character `t ↦ t^p` has orbit map `μ(t)=t^p`, constant differential rank `0`, but image dimension `1`.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-answer.md:170:1. finite maximal algebraically independent subfamily of `{f_i}` has size `trdeg_k k(f_i)`;\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-answer.md:175:6. finite-family rank theorem: `rank span(d f_i) = trdeg_k k(f_i)`;\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-answer.md:179:The single hardest piece is 3-6 as a package: differential theory of finitely generated field extensions, especially the separable algebraic extension step and its use to bridge `AlgebraicIndependent`/`trdeg` with linear independence of Kähler differentials.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-answer.md:181:Verdict on the “secret” dependency: the inequality `trdeg ≤ generic Jacobian rank` does not logically require proving the full theorem `dim_L Ω_{L/k} = trdeg_k L` for every field extension. But it does require the core half of that theory: `Ω` of a rational function field plus injectivity after separably generated extension. In practice, if Mathlib lacks the field-extension `Ω`/`trdeg` bridge, this pulls in a real chunk of infrastructure, not a small wrapper lemma.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/36-A4.2-jacobian-criterion/codex/jacobian-criterion-answer.md:185:Yes: the bound `trdeg ≤ rank δ⁰` is sound if `rank δ⁰` is the generic Jacobian/differential rank over the function field, or if homogeneity proves that this generic rank equals the rank computed at the identity. It is not sound for an arbitrary special point. The most likely naive formalisation break is silently using pointwise rank where generic rank is needed, or assuming `AlgIndependent ↔ LinearIndependent differentials` without first proving the separability/injectivity lemmas for Kähler differentials of field extensions.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/39-hA-codex/codex/hA-run.log:192:./threads/33-A1-kahler-trdeg-api/findings.md:50:| `dim(R/p) = noetherRank s` (s = # alg-indep gens) | `Core.PolynomialDimension.ringKrullDim_quotient_eq_noetherRank` | **PRESENT (landed).** `∃ s ≤ n, (∃ g : k[Fin s] →ₐ[k] (R/p), Inj g ∧ g.IsIntegral) ∧ ringKrullDim (R/p) = (s : WithBot ℕ∞)`. |\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/39-hA-codex/codex/hA-run.log:193:./threads/33-A1-kahler-trdeg-api/findings.md:122:- **Build from scratch:** the `Cardinal`/`Nat` ↔ `WithBot ℕ∞` bookkeeping to land\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/39-hA-codex/codex/hA-run.log:194:./threads/33-A1-kahler-trdeg-api/findings.md:123:  `ringKrullDim(image) = ((trdeg_k image).toNat : WithBot ℕ∞)` (or, cleaner, prove both equal the\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/39-hA-codex/codex/hA-run.log:248:./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/13-L4a-M3-cotangent-regular/codex/cotangent-prompt.md:14:      ringKrullDim (Localization.AtPrime m) = (n : WithBot ℕ∞)\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/39-hA-codex/codex/hA-run.log:249:./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/08-L4-regular-local/codex/sizing-prompt.md:10:  `(p.height : WithBot ℕ∞) + ringKrullDim (R ⧸ p) = n`. (Affine-SPACE equidimensionality only — for the\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/39-hA-codex/codex/hA-run.log:250:./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/05-L5-noether-monic/statement-card.md:83:> - **Gloss.** ideal form: `(p.height : WithBot ℕ∞) + ringKrullDim (R ⧸ p) = (n : WithBot ℕ∞)`.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/39-hA-codex/codex/hA-run.log:251:./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/05-L5-noether-monic/codex/route-prompt.md:4:`Ideal.height p + ringKrullDim (R ⧸ p) = (n : WithBot ℕ∞)`.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/39-hA-codex/codex/hA-run.log:252:./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/05-L5-noether-monic/codex/route-prompt.md:10:- `ringKrullDim_mvPolynomial_fin_field k n : ringKrullDim (MvPolynomial (Fin n) k) = (n:WithBot ℕ∞)`\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/39-hA-codex/codex/hA-run.log:253:./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/05-L5-noether-monic/codex/route-prompt.md:12:- `ringKrullDim_quotient_eq_coheight (p : PrimeSpectrum R) : ringKrullDim (R ⧸ p.asIdeal) = (coheight p : WithBot ℕ∞)`\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/39-hA-codex/codex/hA-run.log:255:./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/05-L5-noether-monic/codex/fidelity-review-answer.md:2:   **OBSERVED:** `height_add_ringKrullDim_quotient_eq` rewrites the quotient dimension by `ringKrullDim_quotient_eq_coheight`, then rewrites prime ideal height to `Order.height`, and discharges from `height_add_coheight_eq`. The latter is an equality in `ℕ∞`, not `WithBot ℕ∞`.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/39-hA-codex/codex/hA-run.log:256:./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/05-L5-noether-monic/codex/fidelity-review-answer.md:4:   **INFERRED:** No hidden `⊥` vacuity. `p.height` is coerced from `ℕ∞`, so it is never `⊥`; for prime quotients, `ringKrullDim (R ⧸ p)` is identified with coerced `coheight`, so also not `⊥`. Since the RHS is finite `(n : WithBot ℕ∞)`, any `⊤` on the LHS would make the equality false, not trivially true. This is a real finite-sum constraint at every prime.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/39-hA-codex/codex/hA-run.log:257:./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/05-L5-noether-monic/codex/route-answer.md:19:`Ideal.height p + ringKrullDim (R ⧸ p) = (n : WithBot ℕ∞)`.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/39-hA-codex/codex/hA-run.log:258:./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/05-L5-noether-monic/codex/route-answer.md:25:- `ringKrullDim_mvPolynomial_fin_field k n : ringKrullDim (MvPolynomial (Fin n) k) = (n:WithBot ℕ∞)`\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/39-hA-codex/codex/hA-run.log:259:./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/05-L5-noether-monic/codex/route-answer.md:27:- `ringKrullDim_quotient_eq_coheight (p : PrimeSpectrum R) : ringKrullDim (R ⧸ p.asIdeal) = (coheight p : WithBot ℕ∞)`\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharg