ent space of the reduced/prime `Z_M` with the chosen minor equations. That does **not** require global determinantal primeness, but it does require either using the vanishing ideal in the bridge or proving the minor generators give the correct first-order equations at `M`.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-stdout.log:7058:6. **Sharpest risk: `Z_M = closure O_M` for equioriented type A.** It balloons if formalized as scheme-theoretic/radical ideal equality or via full Lakshmibai-Magyar/KMS determinantal primeness; keep it as a set-theoretic degeneration-order theorem plus a separate first-order Jacobian lemma.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-stdout.log:7063:1. **No.** Chevalley constructibility exists (`PrimeSpectrum.isConstructible_comap_image`, `Scheme.Hom.isConstructible_image`), and trdeg additivity exists (`Algebra.trdeg` `[stacks 030G]`, `trdeg_add_eq` `[stacks 030H]`), but I found no fibre-dimension theorem / Stacks `02FZ`, `02NM`, `05F6`-usable declaration.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-stdout.log:7070:   - **(b3) Partial, not enough.** Trdeg and Noether normalization exist (`trdeg_add_eq`, `NoetherNormalization.exists_finite_inj_algHom_of_fg` `[stacks 00OW]`), but I found no `ringKrullDim = trdeg` theorem for finitely generated domains.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-stdout.log:7072:4. **No.** Matrix minors/rank infrastructure exists (`Matrix.submatrix`, `Matrix.det`, `Matrix.rank`, `Matrix.rank_submatrix_le`), but I found no determinantal-ideal primeness/radical/CM theory, variety-of-complexes, or quiver-locus ideal package.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-stdout.log:7074:5. **Decision: route (a) is the smaller remaining Lean build, likely by a large factor.** Given your landed smooth/local/Jacobian bedrock, route (a) can avoid full determinantal-ideal primeness if `Z_M = closure O_M` is proved set-theoretically: `O_M` irreducible implies `Z_M` irreducible/prime, and homogeneity plus dense smooth locus gives smoothness of `M`; the genuinely new content is then `Z_M = closure O_M`, smoothness via homogeneity, and `ker Jac_M = range δ⁰`. Route (b) would require building Chevalley fibre dimension plus an algebraic orbit-dimension layer essentially from scratch.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-stdout.log:7076:Caveat: the Jacobian step must compare the cotangent space of the reduced/prime `Z_M` with the chosen minor equations. That does **not** require global determinantal primeness, but it does require either using the vanishing ideal in the bridge or proving the minor generators give the correct first-order equations at `M`.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-stdout.log:7078:6. **Sharpest risk: `Z_M = closure O_M` for equioriented type A.** It balloons if formalized as scheme-theoretic/radical ideal equality or via full Lakshmibai-Magyar/KMS determinantal primeness; keep it as a set-theoretic degeneration-order theorem plus a separate first-order Jacobian lemma.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-prompt.md:15:- The polynomial-ring catenary/dimension formula `height p + ringKrullDim(R/p) = n` for R = k[x_1..x_n].\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-prompt.md:16:- An affine-domain dimension formula `height p + ringKrullDim(A/p) = ringKrullDim A` and\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-prompt.md:17:  local↔global `ringKrullDim(Localization.AtPrime m) = ringKrullDim A` for a finite-type domain A.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-prompt.md:25:- O_M is Zariski-irreducible; the orbit map; vanishingIdeal(image orbit map) = ker(orbit-map pullback).\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-prompt.md:31:ROUTE (a) — \"determinantal / smooth-point\" assembly. Via the landed bridges:\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-prompt.md:32:  varietyDim(Z_M) = ringKrullDim(AtPrime m_M)       [affine-domain local↔global; needs Z_M prime]\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-prompt.md:40:  (the equioriented type-A quiver determinantal-ideal primeness theorem — Lakshmibai–Magyar / Knutson–\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-prompt.md:57:   form usable for affine varieties / finite-type domains over a field (e.g. ringKrullDim relating a\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-prompt.md:58:   morphism's source, target, and fibre; trdeg = ringKrullDim and additivity of trdeg)? Yes/No + the\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-prompt.md:64:   dim(ambient)\" / \"closure of an irreducible preserves Krull dimension\"; (b3) trdeg-based dimension of a\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-prompt.md:66:4. For route (a): is there any determinantal-ideal theory in Mathlib (minors of a generic matrix generate\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-prompt.md:70:   roughly how much? In particular: does route (a) actually need the full determinantal-ideal primeness\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/findings.md:6:- Forward `range δ⁰ ⊆ ker(jacobian)`: easy, unconditional (differentiate `g∘μ_M=0`, `g∈vanishingIdeal(O_M)=ker μ_M^*`\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/findings.md:14:  `vanishingIdeal(Z_M)` as an ideal. Set-equality (Thm 3.8) + Nullstellensatz give only `radical(I_minors) =\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/findings.md:15:  vanishingIdeal(Z_M)`; L2a needs `I_minors = vanishingIdeal(Z_M)` (radical/prime). That is the **equioriented\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/findings.md:16:  type-A quiver determinantal-ideal primeness theorem (Lakshmibai–Magyar Thm 2.2 / Knutson–Miller–Shimozono)** —\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/findings.md:17:  absent in Mathlib v4.29 (matrix minors/rank/Cotangent/Kähler present; NO quiver-determinantal prime/reduced/CM\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/findings.md:20:  determinantal-stratum tangent + barcode/gauge count) is itself a local sub-library on top of the generation gate.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/findings.md:28:`vanishingIdeal(Z_M) = (interval-subproduct minors)` as a prime/radical IDEAL — the Lakshmibai–Magyar/KMS theorem.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/findings.md:29:Gates the determinantal route entirely.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/findings.md:33:### Recommended: SURFACE the scope surprise; pick the sub-library. (a) quiver-determinantal-ideal (Lakshmibai–\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/findings.md:34:Magyar/KMS — SHARES cost with L6, reuses landed `vanishingIdeal(O_M)=ker μ_M^*` + L2a/L4★ → lower marginal cost)\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/codex/l2b-answer.md:3:**(B)** SUB-LIBRARY. FACT: the interval-subproduct minors define the same set as `Z_M`; by Nullstellensatz this gives `vanishingIdeal(Z_M) = radical(I_minors)`, not `I_minors` itself. FACT: L2a needs the stronger scheme-theoretic statement `I_minors = vanishingIdeal(Z_M)`, equivalently radicality/reducedness, and then primeness follows from irreducibility. FACT: for equioriented type A this is the quiver determinantal ideal theorem: orbit closures/quiver loci are scheme-theoretically cut out by these minors and are reduced/Cohen-Macaulay/prime, via Lakshmibai-Magyar/Zelevinsky or Knutson-Miller-Shimozono-type quiver determinantal theory. ([arxiv.org](https://arxiv.org/abs/alg-geom/9709018)) Mathlib v4.29 likely has matrix determinants/rank and commutative algebra infrastructure, but not this quiver determinantal ideal theory.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/codex/l2b-answer.md:5:**(C)** FACT: given the minors, their Jacobian kernel at `M` is the first-order rank-preserving condition for every interval product: for each product `F`, the perturbation `H` satisfies `H(ker F) ⊆ im F`. FACT: in barcode/interval normal form this can be solved uniformly: the interval conditions kill exactly the Ext¹ directions, leaving precisely coboundaries `δ⁰(φ)`. INFERENCE: this is not per-orbit ad hoc, but it is bar/lace-parametrized uniform linear algebra; formalising it still needs a substantial local sub-library: tangent space of determinantal rank strata, differential of subproducts, barcode block decomposition, and the gauge-elimination/Voigt computation.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/codex/l2b-answer.md:11:Verdict: the smallest non-circular route to `varietyDim(Z_M)=finrank(range δ⁰)` is orbit-stabilizer-dimension; determinantal-Jacobian is viable but heavier, and smoothness-only is insufficient. None is bounded in Mathlib v4.29; each real route pulls a missing sub-library.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/codex/l2b-prompt.md:8:  polynomial orbit map μ_M : G → Rep_d, P ↦ P·M). We have PROVED: vanishingIdeal(O_M) = ker(μ_M^*),\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/codex/l2b-prompt.md:24:  REQUIREMENT: g must generate I = vanishingIdeal(Z_M) as an ideal (the family enters as\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/codex/l2b-prompt.md:29:A = k[Rep_d]/vanishingIdeal(Z_M)), THEN:\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/codex/l2b-prompt.md:30:  - ringKrullDim(Localization.AtPrime m_M) = n, where n = finrank of Ω[S/k] on a standard-smooth\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/codex/l2b-prompt.md:33:  - varietyDim(Z_M) = ringKrullDim(AtPrime m_M) = n;\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/codex/l2b-prompt.md:51:    dim O_M = r)? Or is the determinantal/Jacobian-of-minors computation the only non-circular\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/codex/l2b-prompt.md:55:    vanishing ideal vanishingIdeal(Z_M). Are the rank-locus minors — the (r_{ij}+1)×(r_{ij}+1)\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/codex/l2b-prompt.md:56:    minors of the interval sub-products A_j...A_{i+1} — a generating family of vanishingIdeal(Z_M),\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/codex/l2b-prompt.md:57:    i.e. is vanishingIdeal(Z_M) = (those minors) as an ideal (radical/prime)? Is this a bounded,\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/codex/l2b-prompt.md:59:    \"quiver determinantal ideal is prime and minor-generated\" theory? State precisely what is\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/20-L2b-tangent-design/codex/l2b-prompt.md:85:(determinantal-Jacobian / orbit-stabiliser-dimension / smoothness-only) is the smallest\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/33-A1-kahler-trdeg-api/probes/KahlerTrdegProbe.lean:12:Scratch probe (NOT part of the library): pin which trdeg / Kähler / dimension\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/33-A1-kahler-trdeg-api/probes/KahlerTrdegProbe.lean:18:-- ===== Item 2: trdeg API (PRESENT) =====\n./expeditio